# The Windows tier 2 fix (docs/steps/windows-tier2/answered.md): a job A/B
# that runs one side from an archive of its tests, as the Windows test jobs
# do, and the tests' scratch folder those jobs make.

# ------------------------------------------------- a job A/B's archive side

[break] archive-side-named-for-the-other
rule: `--from-archive base` runs the base from an archive, and `head` the head.
file: xtask/src/job_ab.rs
in: parse
find: "base" => Which::Base,
replace: "base" => Which::Head,
caught-by:
    xtask::bin/xtask job_ab::tests::an_archive_side_is_asked_for_by_its_name_and_alone

[break] archive-side-takes-a-package
rule: An archive side takes no `-p` and no nextest arguments: the archive holds the workspace's tests, and its runs are the test jobs' own.
file: xtask/src/job_ab.rs
in: parse
find: && (!request.packages.is_empty() || !request.rest.is_empty())
replace: && (!request.packages.is_empty() && !request.rest.is_empty())
caught-by:
    xtask::bin/xtask job_ab::tests::an_archive_side_is_asked_for_by_its_name_and_alone
    xtask::bin/xtask try_run::tests::a_job_ab_is_test_job_with_against_and_its_options_go_to_ab_job

[break] archive-plan-on-both-sides
rule: Only the side `--from-archive` names runs from an archive; the other builds and runs in one place.
file: xtask/src/job_ab.rs
in: side_plan
find: from_archive: request.from_archive == Some(which)
replace: from_archive: request.from_archive.is_some()
caught-by:
    xtask::bin/xtask job_ab::tests::an_archive_side_is_asked_for_by_its_name_and_alone

[break] archive-runs-tiers-1-and-2-with-the-system-tests
rule: An archive side's first run is tiers 1 and 2 alone, as `test-windows-tiers` runs them.
file: xtask/src/job_ab.rs
in: archive_runs
find: from_archive_run(tree, &format!("not {SYSTEM_TESTS}"))
replace: from_archive_run(tree, "all()")
caught-by:
    xtask::bin/xtask job_ab::tests::an_archive_side_runs_the_windows_test_jobs_runs_from_its_archive

[break] archive-side-build-left-aside-by-a-clean
rule: A clean takes an archive side's set-aside build too, so that a cold round builds from nothing.
file: xtask/src/job_ab.rs
find: for folder in ["ci", BUILT_ASIDE, "tmp"] {
replace: for folder in ["ci", "tmp"] {
caught-by:
    xtask::bin/xtask job_ab::tests::an_archive_sides_build_is_set_aside_and_put_back

[break] try-drops-the-archive-side
rule: `try`'s `test --job --from-archive SIDE` passes the side on to `ab --job`.
file: xtask/src/try_run.rs
in: job_ab
find: command.extend(["--from-archive".to_owned(), side]);
replace: let _ = side;
caught-by:
    xtask::bin/xtask try_run::tests::a_job_ab_is_test_job_with_against_and_its_options_go_to_ab_job

[break] after-the-round-never-called
rule: A side's work after its round (an archive side's build put back) is done once its figures are taken, whatever the round did, and outside `the job`.
file: xtask/src/job_ab.rs
in: drive_side
find: phases.after_round();
replace: let _ = &phases;
caught-by:
    xtask::bin/xtask job_ab::tests::a_side_times_each_phase_and_a_failed_build_ends_its_round
    xtask::bin/xtask job_ab::tests::an_archive_sides_extraction_is_timed_after_its_build_and_a_failed_one_ends_the_round

[break] archive-side-build-never-put-back
rule: After its round an archive side puts its build back in its place, so that its next build is warm and the tree is left as it was built.
file: xtask/src/job_ab.rs
find: let Err(error) = put_back(self.tree)
replace: let Err(error) = Ok::<(), String>(())
caught-by:
    xtask::bin/xtask job_ab::tests::an_archive_side_puts_its_build_back_after_its_round_and_the_other_side_touches_nothing

# ------------------------------------------- the test jobs' scratch folder

[break] tests-scratch-folder-under-the-profile
rule: A test job that runs from the archive makes the folder cargo gives the tests as `CARGO_TARGET_TMPDIR`, `target/tmp`, not a profile's.
file: xtask/src/checks.rs
in: tests_tmp_dir
find: root.join("target").join("tmp")
replace: root.join("target").join("ci").join("tmp")
caught-by:
    xtask::bin/xtask checks::tests::the_tests_scratch_folder_is_the_target_directorys_own
